module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteEtaleColimits.CoequalizerBaseChange
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FundamentalGroup.GaloisCategories.Defs
import all StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FundamentalGroup.EtaleFundamental.GaloisCategoryAxioms
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# The finite étale covers of a connected scheme form a Galois category

Let `X` be a connected scheme and let `x` be a geometric point of `X`. This file proves that the
geometric fibre functor `F_x : FÉt_X ⥤ Type` **preserves finite colimits**, and deduces that
`FÉt_X` together with `F_x` satisfies all six axioms of
`CategoryTheory.IsGaloisCategory`.

Five of the six axioms are proved in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FundamentalGroup/EtaleFundamental/GaloisCategoryAxioms.lean`,
whose implementation notes record the sixth — the colimit half of exactness of `F_x` — as needing
exactly one input: `PreservesFiniteColimits (finiteEtaleBaseChange x.hom)`, the fourth assertion
of Stacks Tag 0BN9. That is now
`Stacks.FundamentalGroup.preservesFiniteColimits_finiteEtaleBaseChange`, so the deduction is the
factorisation `F_x ≅ (base change along x) ⋙ (the functor corepresented by the identity cover of
the point)` of `AlgebraicGeometry.fiberIsoPointCoyoneda`, whose second factor preserves all
finite colimits.

## Main results

* `Stacks.FundamentalGroup.preservesFiniteColimits_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor` — **the geometric
  fibre functor preserves finite colimits.**
* `Stacks.FundamentalGroup.isGaloisCategory_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor` — **Stacks Tag 0BNB: the
  category of finite étale covers of a connected scheme, with a geometric fibre functor, is a
  Galois category.**

## Implementation notes

The covering set of Tag 0BNB is the single instance asserting the six axioms, namely
`Stacks.FundamentalGroup.isGaloisCategory_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor`.

`AlgebraicGeometry.fiberIsoPointCoyoneda` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.pointCoyoneda_preservesFiniteColimits` are `private` in the file that proves
them, so that file is imported with `import all` rather than having its helpers re-proved here;
this is the same route that
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FiniteEtaleColimits/BaseChangeCoproducts.lean` takes for the
coproduct half.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BN9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BN9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BNB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BNB)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.FundamentalGroup

/-- **The geometric fibre functor preserves coequalizers.** Through the factorisation
`AlgebraicGeometry.fiberIsoPointCoyoneda` of the fibre functor as base change along the
geometric point followed by the functor corepresented by the identity cover of the point, the
first factor preserves coequalizers by
`Stacks.FundamentalGroup.preservesColimitsOfShape_walkingParallelPair_finiteEtaleBaseChange` and
the second preserves all finite colimits. -/
@[sga "1 XIII 2.1.3" "Clause of G5"]
theorem preservesColimitsOfShape_walkingParallelPair_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (x : GeometricPoint X) :
    PreservesColimitsOfShape WalkingParallelPair (finiteEtaleFiberFunctor x) := by
  have hco : PreservesFiniteColimits
      (coyoneda.obj (op (finiteEtalePointId x.residueField))) :=
    pointCoyoneda_preservesFiniteColimits x.residueField
  have hcomp : PreservesColimitsOfShape WalkingParallelPair
      (finiteEtaleBaseChange x.hom ⋙
        coyoneda.obj (op (finiteEtalePointId x.residueField))) := inferInstance
  exact preservesColimitsOfShape_of_natIso (fiberIsoPointCoyoneda x).symm

/-- **Stacks 0BNB, the colimit half of exactness: the geometric fibre functor preserves
finite colimits.** Finite colimits of `FÉt_X` are generated by its finite coproducts, which the
fibre functor preserves by
`Stacks.FundamentalGroup.preservesFiniteCoproducts_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor`, and its
coequalizers, which it preserves by
`Stacks.FundamentalGroup.preservesColimitsOfShape_walkingParallelPair_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor`. -/
theorem preservesFiniteColimits_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (x : GeometricPoint X) : PreservesFiniteColimits (finiteEtaleFiberFunctor x) :=
  have := preservesColimitsOfShape_walkingParallelPair_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor x
  preservesFiniteColimits_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor_of_preservesCoequalizers x

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0BNB.** For a connected scheme `X` and a geometric point `x` of `X`,
the category `FÉt_X` of finite étale covers of `X` together with the geometric fibre functor
`F_x` is a Galois category.

The six axioms are: finite limits and finite colimits of `FÉt_X`
(`Stacks.FundamentalGroup.hasFiniteLimits_finiteEtaleOver` and
`Stacks.FundamentalGroup.hasFiniteColimits_finiteEtaleOver`); every cover is a finite coproduct
of connected ones (`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_finiteCoproduct_isConnected_finiteEtaleOver`);
finiteness of every geometric fibre (`AlgebraicGeometry.finite_finiteEtaleFiber`); that `F_x`
reflects isomorphisms (`AlgebraicGeometry.reflectsIsomorphisms_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor`); and
exactness of `F_x`, whose limit half is
`AlgebraicGeometry.preservesFiniteLimits_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor` and whose colimit half is
`Stacks.FundamentalGroup.preservesFiniteColimits_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor`. -/
@[stacks 0BNB,
  sga "1 V 3.7" "more general",
  sga "1 XIII 2.1.3" "(C_t, special case",
  sga "3 X 7.0.3" "special case",
  sga "5 VI 1.2.3.1"]
instance isGaloisCategory_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor {X : Scheme.{u}} [ConnectedSpace X]
    (x : GeometricPoint X) : IsGaloisCategory (finiteEtaleFiberFunctor x) where
  hasFiniteLimits := hasFiniteLimits_finiteEtaleOver X
  hasFiniteColimits := hasFiniteColimits_finiteEtaleOver X
  exists_finite_coproduct_connected := exists_finiteCoproduct_isConnected_finiteEtaleOver x
  finite_obj := finite_finiteEtaleFiber x
  reflectsIsomorphisms := reflectsIsomorphisms_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor x
  exact :=
    ⟨preservesFiniteLimits_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor x,
      preservesFiniteColimits_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor x⟩

end Stacks.FundamentalGroup

end
